1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,290
Step two was the last step I built.

2
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:04,470
It runs second, and I wrote it last.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,070
So what were the other steps
doing while it was missing?

4
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:09,090
Here is the setup.

5
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:12,730
In a public repository called
Mycroft, a recipe is a list of steps,

6
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:14,550
each with a script behind it.

7
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:17,610
Mine fetches prices for five
stocks and adds them up.

8
00:00:17,820 --> 00:00:20,190
I built step one, then three, then five,

9
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:22,630
four and six much later,
and step two last.

10
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:26,210
Tanmay Kulkarni, for Humanitarians AI.

11
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:29,670
In my recipe I wrote that step
three reads the files directly,

12
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,310
since step two is still open.

13
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:35,370
And that step five reads step three's
output, since step four is still open.

14
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:39,050
Those are stand-ins: shortcuts
for steps that did not exist yet.

15
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:43,270
So I gave them a wrong file
deliberately, on a scratch copy.

16
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,750
In the NVDA price file I
switched two digits around:

17
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:52,730
504.5625 became 540.5625. Still a number.

18
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,030
Still valid JSON.

19
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:00,110
Step one stopped. But step three, on its
own, said pass: 5 promoted, none rejected.

20
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:05,850
And step five priced the
portfolio at $66,898,

21
00:01:05,870 --> 00:01:07,030
$1,800 more than the real run.

22
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:10,370
Then the real step two
read the same folder.

23
00:01:10,580 --> 00:01:14,310
It checks each file against a hash
recorded when the sample files were made.

24
00:01:14,520 --> 00:01:17,590
It turned the file away: it differs
from the hash in the manifest.

25
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,030
The same wrong file,
through a different door.

26
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:23,970
I want to be fair to the old
route. Step one did stop.

27
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:28,290
And this was a scratch copy of invented
prices, one swapped pair, in one recipe.

28
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,870
My claim is only that step
three, on its own, cannot know.

29
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,590
So write down your stand-ins,
and what each one skipped.

30
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:38,830
Then give the stand-in and the
real step the same wrong input.

31
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:42,130
The long film is called Step
Two Was the Last One I Built.
